# Agent workflow

- Read `AGENTS.md` before making changes. Also read `PROJECT_STATUS.md`, `ROADMAP.md` and relevant ADRs when they exist.
- Check the relevant roadmap item and acceptance criteria.
- For non-trivial work, present a plan before editing files.
- Run relevant validation commands and report their actual results.
- Update documentation and project status after completing verified work.
- Keep `PROJECT_STATUS.md` scoped to the **current phase** (progress, acceptance, latest validation, active decision gates). Do not rebuild cumulative Delivered/Verified/full Open-decisions tables. Issue backlog stays in `ROADMAP.md`; full decisions in `DECISIONS.md`; older narrative in `docs/status-log.md`.
- Put verified numbers, commands, and results in architecture docs / ADRs / `docs/status-log.md`. Do not cite `PROJECT_STATUS.md` as durable evidence from other docs — that ledger is rewritten and those links go stale.
- Do not silently change architecture, dependencies or acceptance criteria.
- Do not mark a task complete unless its acceptance criteria have been verified.
- Record what was implemented and what the checks showed. Do not record pauses, retries, or other recovery steps that do not change how to operate the result.
- An entry point that belongs to the issue and was not run is not verified. Name it and say why before treating the issue as done.
- At the end of every task, report: objective, files changed, commands run, tests (passed and failed), acceptance criteria, limitations and the suggested next issue.
